  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zimbabwe Resilience Programme Joint Funded by DFID, EU and UNDP  -  Managed by UNDP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZRBF is designed to improve the resilience of about 830,000 people by i) Building evidence to improve the policy environment and stimulate service provision to enhance household and community resilience; ii) supporting projects that improve absorptive, adaptive and transformative capacities of target communities ; and iii) providing a risk financing mechanism (&#x201C;crisis modifier&#x201D;) that enables early action in response to early warning of crises in order to protect the development gains of the fund.</narrative>
  </description>
